{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "eno1_minmod",
    "description": "Pointwise first-order ENO (minmod) selection of a one-sided derivative from the backward difference dl = (u[i]-u[i-1])/h and the forward difference dr = (u[i+1]-u[i])/h: the smaller-magnitude one when both have the same sign, zero when they disagree in sign (the derivative crosses zero inside the cell) or either vanishes. Written without sign() or a branch as max(0, min(dl, dr)) + min(0, max(dl, dr)): for dl, dr > 0 this is min(dl, dr); for dl, dr < 0 it is max(dl, dr) (the less negative); for mixed signs or a zero operand both terms vanish -- identical to fire_behavior's Select_eno (if dl*dr > 0 then sign(dl) min(|dl|,|dr|) else 0). First order O(h) on smooth data (a one-sided difference), exact on a linear field (dl = dr = a gives a), total-variation-diminishing through kinks. Match-less helper bound by the weno5_eno1_* stencils and rules of this grid.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:limiter",
      "axes:x",
      "order:1",
      "stencil_width:3"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Harten, A., Engquist, B., Osher, S., & Chakravarthy, S. R. (1987). Uniformly high order accurate essentially non-oscillatory schemes, III. Journal of Computational Physics, 71(2), 231-303. ENO stencil selection by smallest divided difference (first-order form: the minmod limiter).",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(87)90031-3"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls, Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Select_godunov (case 4), Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [],
  "expression_templates": {
    "eno1_minmod": {
      "params": [
        "dl",
        "dr"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
              0,
              {
                "op": "min",
                "args": [
                  "dl",
                  "dr"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "min",
            "args": [
              0,
              {
                "op": "max",
                "args": [
                  "dl",
                  "dr"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
